From: Korri <korri@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] input/hog-lib: read the Report Map after "Attribute Not Found"

The GameSir-G8+ answers reads of its Report values and of their CCC
descriptors with "Attribute Not Found". hog-lib read the Report Map only
when the last outstanding request succeeded, so it never read it, never
created the uhid device, and dropped the notifications the controller
was already sending.

Also read it when the last request failed with Attribute Not Found, and
only while the device is still attached. Any other error (for example a
request cancelled on disconnect) keeps the old behaviour: an earlier
version of this patch read the Report Map after every error and crashed
bluetoothd when requests were cancelled on detach.
---
--- a/profiles/input/hog-lib.c
+++ b/profiles/input/hog-lib.c
@@ -159,7 +159,12 @@
 
 	queue_remove(hog->gatt_op, req);
 
-	if (!status && queue_isempty(hog->gatt_op)) {
+	/* Some devices (GameSir-G8+) answer reads of Report values and their
+	 * CCC descriptors with Attribute Not Found. Treat that as done, so the
+	 * Report Map is still read and the uhid device is created.
+	 */
+	if ((!status || status == ATT_ECODE_ATTR_NOT_FOUND) && hog->attrib &&
+					queue_isempty(hog->gatt_op)) {
 		/* Report Map must be read last since that can result
 		 * in uhid being created and the driver may start to
 		 * use UHID_SET_REPORT which requires the report->id to
